<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!--
  The world a recording run flies in. Chunk 3.6.

  It is worlds/uavx_empty.world with one static camera added, and it is a
  separate file rather than an addition to that one for a plain reason: every
  gated scenario runs in uavx_empty.world, none of them needs a camera, and
  rendering one costs real time under software OpenGL. The runs already
  archived were flown without it and the ones week 4 flies should match them.

  Why a camera in the world at all. The video is a deliverable and the only
  capture path this stack has. gzclient has taken this WSL distribution down
  three times and is never launched, so there is no window to record; the
  frames have to come from a sensor gzserver renders itself. Measured on 5
  September 2026 before any of this was written: gzserver renders a camera
  sensor headless here at about 7 Hz against a requested 10, publishes it on a
  ROS image topic, and the frames are of the scene rather than blank.

  Where it stands and why. The swarm occupies x 0 to 475 and y -75 to +75 at
  30 to 60 m, per the common geometry table in architecture.md section 6. From
  (-120, 0, 50) the axis is aimed just above level so the chain sits across the
  middle of the frame rather than above it: the anchor is 285 m ahead and 20 m
  below the axis, and the far pair are 595 m ahead, level, and 0.13 rad either
  side of it. All four are inside the 0.7 by 0.39 rad field.

  The first attempt used a 1.2 rad field and 0.10 rad of down pitch, which put
  the whole chain in the sky above the horizon and every vehicle at about one
  pixel. Narrowing the field and aiming it level brought the vehicles into
  frame and the shot was still empty, because model://ground_plane is a hundred
  metres across and the swarm stands 285 to 595 m away over nothing at all.

  Hence the two models below. A wide apron under the corridor and a centre line
  down it, both visual only with no collision geometry, so nothing about the
  flight changes and the physics is the physics every other scenario flies.
  They give the shot a horizon, a scale and somewhere for the eye to measure
  distance against, and they exist in this world and in no other.

  One static camera still cannot make a 480 m formation of half metre vehicles
  fill a frame, and relay_required has nothing moving in it for 240 s. The demo
  shot belongs to mission_integrated, and that is recorded in
  docs/progress/week-3.md rather than solved here.

  The camera is not a sensor any process may reason about. It publishes an
  image and nothing else reads it but the harness, and scripts/check_seam.sh
  holds it to that: /uavx_record/uavx_camera_plugin is an outside process with
  two publishers and no subscribers.
-->
<sdf version="1.5">
  <world name="default">
    <!-- A global light source -->
    <include>
      <uri>model://sun</uri>
    </include>
    <!-- A ground plane -->
    <include>
      <uri>model://ground_plane</uri>
    </include>
    <include>
      <uri>model://asphalt_plane</uri>
    </include>
    <physics name='default_physics' default='0' type='ode'>
      <gravity>0 0 -9.8066</gravity>
      <ode>
        <solver>
          <type>quick</type>
          <iters>10</iters>
          <sor>1.3</sor>
          <use_dynamic_moi_rescaling>0</use_dynamic_moi_rescaling>
        </solver>
        <constraints>
          <cfm>0</cfm>
          <erp>0.2</erp>
          <contact_max_correcting_vel>100</contact_max_correcting_vel>
          <contact_surface_layer>0.001</contact_surface_layer>
        </constraints>
      </ode>
      <max_step_size>0.004</max_step_size>
      <real_time_factor>1</real_time_factor>
      <real_time_update_rate>250</real_time_update_rate>
      <magnetic_field>6.0e-6 2.3e-5 -4.2e-5</magnetic_field>
    </physics>

    <plugin name="gazebo_ros_state" filename="libgazebo_ros_state.so">
      <ros>
        <namespace>/gazebo</namespace>
      </ros>
      <update_rate>50.0</update_rate>
    </plugin>

    <!--
      Scenery, and only for the camera. No collision geometry anywhere below,
      so these cannot touch a vehicle, change a contact or alter a solver
      step. The apron runs the length of the corridor the swarm occupies,
      x 0 to 475 with margin either end, and the line down the middle is what
      makes the distance readable.
    -->
    <model name="uavx_record_apron">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>240 0 0.02 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <visual name="apron">
          <geometry><box><size>1400 600 0.04</size></box></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.32 0.34 0.30 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.42 0.45 0.39 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="uavx_record_centreline">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>240 0 0.05 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <visual name="line">
          <geometry><box><size>1000 3 0.02</size></box></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.75 0.72 0.55 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.88 0.85 0.65 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="uavx_record_camera">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>-120 0 50 0 0.035 0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <sensor name="view" type="camera">
          <update_rate>10.0</update_rate>
          <always_on>1</always_on>
          <camera>
            <horizontal_fov>0.7</horizontal_fov>
            <image>
              <width>960</width>
              <height>540</height>
              <format>R8G8B8</format>
            </image>
            <clip>
              <near>1.0</near>
              <far>3000</far>
            </clip>
          </camera>
          <plugin name="uavx_camera_plugin" filename="libgazebo_ros_camera.so">
            <ros>
              <namespace>/uavx_record</namespace>
            </ros>
            <camera_name>view</camera_name>
            <frame_name>uavx_record_camera</frame_name>
          </plugin>
        </sensor>
      </link>
    </model>
  </world>
</sdf>
